rove the quality of the hypothesis space.', 'Data_Centric_Foundation: Conduct a detailed dataset analysis to form a comprehensive dataset profile. Construct multimer data and baseline models, and construct 3D structural data and baseline models. For graph representation learning, perform a benchmark analysis on the impact of node and edge feature dimensions on model performance. This lays a solid and comprehensive foundation for subsequent research.', 'Advanced Algorithm Improvement: Improve current state-of-the-art molecular property prediction algorithms, such as DMPNN, Graph Transformer, and Long Short Range Message Passing, based on a deep understanding of their underlying mechanisms, making them better align with algorithmic or physical prior assumptions to achieve better results.', 'Self-Supervised Pretraining: Fully utilize multimer data and 3D structural data to conduct monomer versus multimer contrastive learning or 2D-3D contrastive learning, embedding polymer prior features into network weights to achieve better results.'], 'daily_journal': [{'day': 1, 'journal': '**Day 1 Journal: Tg Prediction - Initial Experiments**\n\n**Papers Selected and Analyzed:**\nSelected 4 papers following MetaMethod criteria: LSR-MP (physics-informed long-short range separation), Periodic Graphs for Polymers (polymer graph with periodic edge), FragNet (4-level interpretability), and PerioGT (current SOTA). Saved comprehensive analyses to mem_073-076. Key insight: PerioGT achieves RMSE=30.8 via periodicity-aware pretraining, establishing the target to beat.\n\n**Experiments Conducted:**\nRan 3 iterations on Tg dataset (7170 samples, 72/8/20 split) attempting to beat SOTA:\n\n- **v1 (Hierarchical PPFN):** Combined periodic edge, fragment attention, and long-range bipartite module. Result: RMSE 37.36. Architecture too complex initially.\n\n- **v2 (Simplified):** Removed complexity, used GINE only with periodic edge. Result: RMSE 36.74. Ablation showed periodic edge provided only ~